    "Optional emphasis markers at the two intersection points of the radial line with the circle (r = 2) and with the cardioid (r = 2(1+cosθ))",
    "Curve legend implied by color: blue = inner boundary r = 2, purple = outer boundary r = f(θ)",
    "Readout text showing current θ, inner r, and outer r for the radial strip"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "outerBoundary",
      "type": "equation_input",
      "teaches": "The outer boundary formula alone decides where the two curves meet and therefore how wide the first-quadrant region R is and what the inner limit of integration must be.",
      "label": "Outer polar boundary r = f(θ)",
      "fields": [
        {
          "id": "fTheta",
          "label": "r = f(θ) =",
          "default": "2*(1+cos(theta))",
          "variables": ["theta"],
