    {
      "title": "The two boundaries",
      "narration": "The blue circle r = 2 and the purple cardioid r = 2(1 + cos θ) both start at the top point (0, 2) and separate as θ decreases toward 0. Between them, in the first quadrant, lies the region R.",
      "state": { "thetaSweep": 0, "regionView": "Full region R" }
    },
    {
      "title": "One radial strip",
      "narration": "At a fixed angle θ, the red ray enters R at the circle (r = 2) and leaves at the cardioid (r = 2(1 + cos θ)). Those two crossings are the inner limits of the integral.",
