  "concept": "In polar coordinates a region bounded between two curves is swept by a radial strip whose inner and outer ends are r = 2 and r = 2(1+cosθ), which is exactly what the inner limits of the iterated integral encode.",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Horizontal polar axis (θ = 0 ray) drawn as a black line through the origin, labeled 'θ = 0' to the right of the origin",
